# What does not belong in the build context. Everything here either makes the
# image bigger or makes it wrong: node_modules of another platform, a dist
# from yesterday, or a .env holding real credentials.

.git/
.github/
.turbo/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
# The build of the preview, which lets every request through. Never in an
# image, not even in the build stage.
**/preview-build/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log

# None of this is built or shipped.
docs/
docker/
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
LICENSE

# assets/ is shipped: it is the public folder of the interface build
# (publicDir in packages/web/vite.config.ts), which copies what is in it into
# the interface, so assets/brand is what the image serves under /brand. Left
# out of the context, the image of 0.1.0 had no favicon and no icon at all,
# and nothing failed (#213). Only the README next to the brand files stays
# out; it is written for people, not for browsers.
assets/brand/README.md
